<< /Alt (Figure 17.4: What happens to these functions as the index grows? For n=4, the peak is \(1/4,4\), support ends at 2/4, supremum is 4, exact integral is 1, and f_n\(1/2\)=0. For every fixed x>0, eventually x>2/n; f_n\(0\)=0. The pointwise limit is zero, but the integrals stay one. The graph is finite evidence; the vertex and area formulas prove the claims.) /K 7 /P 33095 0 R /Pg 3902 0 R /S /Figure /Type /StructElem >>
endobj
